1
00:00:01,350 --> 00:00:04,167
Every shift on a mine starts with the same question.

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:08,603
What is actually in the ore we're sending to the plant today?

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,121
Geologists log the core,

4
00:00:11,151 --> 00:00:15,095
and a handheld XRF reads the elements: nickel, copper, chrome,

5
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:15,997
sulphur.

6
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:19,309
But elements are not minerals.

7
00:00:19,339 --> 00:00:22,045
XRF can't tell you which mineral carries the nickel,

8
00:00:22,075 --> 00:00:23,908
or whether that grain will float free,

9
00:00:23,938 --> 00:00:25,553
or stay locked in rock.

10
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,129
That answer lives in the grains.

11
00:00:29,159 --> 00:00:32,625
So a polished section goes under a reflected-light microscope,

12
00:00:33,290 --> 00:00:35,294
and the image goes to REEFPRINT.

13
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:38,317
Open it on a laptop in the bakkie.

14
00:00:38,347 --> 00:00:40,546
On a phone at the core yard.

15
00:00:40,576 --> 00:00:42,604
At a desk in the plant office.

16
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:46,858
This is REEFPRINT, also known as KHANYA.

17
00:00:46,888 --> 00:00:49,398
Mineral intelligence from a micrograph.

18
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:54,091
The dashboard puts the specimen library,

19
00:00:54,121 --> 00:00:57,508
model readiness and recorded evidence in one view.

20
00:00:57,538 --> 00:01:01,717
These are held-out LumenStone S2 sections: public data, from nickel,

21
00:01:01,747 --> 00:01:04,034
copper and PGE sulphide ore.

22
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:07,421
Choose a section and run the analysis.

23
00:01:07,451 --> 00:01:12,692
A DeepLabV3 network classifies six fields on an ordinary laptop CPU.

24
00:01:12,722 --> 00:01:17,810
No cloud, no GPU. Every tile you see is real model output,

25
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:18,995
sped up here.

26
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:22,920
Deliverable one: mineral phases. Pyrrhotite,

27
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:24,819
pentlandite and chalcopyrite,

28
00:01:24,849 --> 00:01:26,281
mapped pixel by pixel,

29
00:01:26,311 --> 00:01:28,244
with the area fraction of each.

30
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:30,551
Every result carries its model,

31
00:01:30,581 --> 00:01:33,249
its checkpoint hash and its runtime.

32
00:01:33,279 --> 00:01:35,937
Confidence is shown, and labelled uncalibrated,

33
00:01:35,967 --> 00:01:37,063
because it is.

34
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,736
Click any grain for its size,

35
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:44,038
its composition, and whether the valuable mineral is free, or locked.

36
00:01:44,068 --> 00:01:47,593
That's liberation: the question a metallurgist actually asks.

37
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:53,220
Attach an XRF or lab assay to compare the chemistry with the phase map.

38
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:55,543
XRF measures elements.

39
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:57,459
REEFPRINT maps minerals.

40
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:00,591
Deliverable two: the accuracy report,

41
00:02:00,621 --> 00:02:02,923
bound to the exact checkpoint.

42
00:02:02,953 --> 00:02:04,810
Across twelve held-out sections,

43
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:10,600
mean IoU is 0.454, and pixel accuracy seventy-seven percent.

44
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,286
Magnetite scores zero,

45
00:02:12,316 --> 00:02:13,872
and the report says so.

46
00:02:14,430 --> 00:02:18,834
A retrained candidate records 0.632 on the same twelve sections,

47
00:02:18,864 --> 00:02:20,827
and now finds most of the magnetite,

48
00:02:20,857 --> 00:02:23,336
but with too many false alarms.

49
00:02:23,366 --> 00:02:24,881
So it stays quarantined,

50
00:02:24,911 --> 00:02:26,903
and the live model is unchanged.

51
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:31,527
Deliverable three: from mineralogy to a plant parameter.

52
00:02:31,557 --> 00:02:34,970
The advisory reads a forty-one percent sulphide association,

53
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,885
inside the uncertainty band around the fifty percent floor.

54
00:02:38,915 --> 00:02:41,438
So it says: verify before acting.

55
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:43,909
Test the setpoint in the simulator.

56
00:02:43,939 --> 00:02:46,091
This checkpoint isn't approved for control,

57
00:02:46,121 --> 00:02:48,048
so the setting is held.

58
00:02:48,078 --> 00:02:49,451
When the evidence is thin,

59
00:02:49,481 --> 00:02:52,110
REEFPRINT refuses, rather than guesses.

60
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:56,840
Every decision exports as a traceable record: the result,

61
00:02:56,870 --> 00:02:59,581
the checkpoint, and the simulator's response.

62
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:03,867
Spatial ties samples to survey coordinates, plan maps,

63
00:03:03,897 --> 00:03:08,365
sections and 3D, with synthetic geometry clearly marked as synthetic.

64
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:12,334
And the evidence companion answers questions about the selected result,

65
00:03:12,364 --> 00:03:13,514
labelling what's measured,

66
00:03:13,544 --> 00:03:16,019
what's predicted, and what's simulated.

67
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:19,814
The same workbench, in your pocket.

68
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:24,157
Three mineral phases identified.

69
00:03:24,187 --> 00:03:27,435
An accuracy report, with every number traced.

70
00:03:27,465 --> 00:03:30,271
And a path to the plant that knows when not to act.

71
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:34,728
REEFPRINT. Built by Team Sonar.
